WEBVTT

00:01.001 --> 00:03.920
WRITTEN BY HYUGA NATSU

01:32.592 --> 01:33.426
THIS STORY IS A FICTION AND ALL NAMES OF
FIGURES AND ORGANIZATIONS ARE FICTITIOUS.

01:33.510 --> 01:34.552
MOREOVER, THE STORY HAS NO RELATION
TO REAL-LIFE INCIDENTS AND EVENTS.

01:34.636 --> 01:36.805
Let me introduce them to you, Maomao.

01:36.888 --> 01:39.682
These are the new attendants
at the Jade Pavilion.

01:39.766 --> 01:40.850
They’re three sisters.

01:41.851 --> 01:43.228
I’m Haku-u.

01:43.311 --> 01:44.646
I’m Koku-u.

01:44.729 --> 01:45.605
I’m Seki-u.

01:46.356 --> 01:48.108
<i>They really do look alike…</i>

01:49.067 --> 01:50.819
How have you been?

01:50.902 --> 01:52.654
Fine. It’s been a while.

01:54.280 --> 01:55.698
Do you know each other?

01:55.782 --> 01:59.077
Yes, we’re from the same hometown
and are familiar with each other.

01:59.160 --> 02:00.411
The eldest, Haku-u,

02:00.495 --> 02:02.789
is the same age as Lady Gyokuyou.

02:04.040 --> 02:07.043
<i>So they're surrounding her</i>
<i>only with people from her hometown?</i>

02:07.127 --> 02:10.004
<i>For Lady Gyokuyou</i>
<i>who has been nearly assassinated before,</i>

02:10.088 --> 02:11.923
<i>this arrangement would be safer.</i>

02:12.715 --> 02:13.675
And you are?

02:14.300 --> 02:16.761
I am Maomao, the food taster, Lady Koku-u.

02:17.595 --> 02:19.764
I'm not Koku-u.

02:19.848 --> 02:22.308
Oh, then you must be Lady Seki-u…

02:22.892 --> 02:23.768
I’m Haku-u.

02:28.565 --> 02:32.360
From now on, we’ll wear
hair ribbons that match our names.

02:32.443 --> 02:35.321
-Then you can tell us apart.
-Understood.

02:36.406 --> 02:39.117
<i>I really can’t tell them apart…</i>

02:39.200 --> 02:41.494
<i>Well, I guess</i>
<i>I’ll figure it out over time.</i>

02:42.537 --> 02:44.706
<i>But more importantly…</i>

02:44.789 --> 02:45.665
Maomao!

02:45.748 --> 02:47.917
Return to your designated room!

02:48.001 --> 02:50.962
No, the storage room is fine for me.

02:51.045 --> 02:54.048
Even Lady Hongniang told me
this is my room,

02:54.132 --> 02:56.009
so I’ll continue using it as it is.

02:56.092 --> 02:58.428
I will not allow that!

02:58.511 --> 03:01.180
You took that joke
too seriously once again!

03:01.848 --> 03:05.602
But I’ve already moved
all my belongings here…

03:05.685 --> 03:08.646
It wouldn’t set a good example
for the new attendants!

03:12.400 --> 03:15.028
What are you two doing?!

03:27.165 --> 03:28.166
Oh my.

03:28.249 --> 03:31.252
Has the storage room
completely turned into Maomao’s nest?

03:32.211 --> 03:34.005
You can do as you like with the shed.

03:34.923 --> 03:38.509
But when you sleep,
please use your designated room.

03:39.093 --> 03:39.969
Understood.

03:41.596 --> 03:43.389
<i>They’re such kind superiors.</i>

03:47.810 --> 03:49.437
<i>With the arrival of new attendants,</i>

03:49.520 --> 03:52.774
<i>the workload per person</i>
<i>has significantly decreased.</i>

03:53.524 --> 03:55.443
<i>With Lady Gyokuyou expecting a child,</i>

03:55.526 --> 03:59.322
<i>the Jade Pavilion will need</i>
<i>even more hands.</i>

03:59.405 --> 04:02.283
<i>So reinforcing the workforce</i>
<i>is certainly a good thing…</i>

04:03.284 --> 04:05.912
<i>But this is also likely an effort</i>
<i>to balance things out</i>

04:05.995 --> 04:10.250
<i>with Lady Loulan’s Garnet Pavilion,</i>
<i>which has a large number of maids.</i>

04:12.543 --> 04:13.503
Thanks for your hard work.

04:14.462 --> 04:16.381
Well then, I’ll head to the shed.

04:17.298 --> 04:18.424
Maomao!

04:19.550 --> 04:22.303
Lady Yinghua,
does Maomao really live in a shed,

04:22.387 --> 04:24.305
instead of a proper room?

04:24.389 --> 04:27.517
Is that true? Even though
she’s Lady Gyokuyou’s attendant?

04:27.600 --> 04:29.978
Well…

04:43.741 --> 04:46.869
<i>The reason Lady Yinghua is trying to stop</i>
<i>me from shutting myself away in the shed</i>

04:46.953 --> 04:50.873
<i>is because</i>
<i>she’s looking out for my well-being.</i>

04:50.957 --> 04:54.127
<i>She wants me to quickly feel at ease with</i>
<i>the new attendants.</i>

04:54.210 --> 04:55.837
<i>It’s a reflection of her thoughtfulness.</i>

05:01.968 --> 05:04.512
I’m sorry for acting so selfishly.

05:04.595 --> 05:06.472
It’s fine, but…

05:06.556 --> 05:09.475
Hey, Maomao, do you feel
even a little remorse?

05:09.559 --> 05:11.269
Huh? I do, of course.

05:11.352 --> 05:13.855
Really? Do you actually feel bad?

05:14.355 --> 05:15.398
Yes, of course…

05:15.481 --> 05:17.108
I thought so!

05:17.191 --> 05:20.611
Then tonight, you’re coming with me!

05:21.404 --> 05:24.866
Tonight, the only ones free are
you and me, Maomao!

05:24.949 --> 05:27.243
How convenient!

05:30.163 --> 05:31.622
<i>I walked right into that…</i>

05:36.961 --> 05:40.006
Uh, about going out tonight,
what did Lady Hongniang say?

05:40.089 --> 05:42.967
It’s fine. I already got her permission.

05:43.718 --> 05:45.720
<i>The north side of the rear palace…</i>

05:47.430 --> 05:50.349
<i>There should only be</i>
<i>old buildings around here.</i>

05:53.436 --> 05:54.395
Maomao, here.

05:55.146 --> 05:56.856
Put this on like this.

05:58.900 --> 06:00.151
Isn’t this hot?

06:00.234 --> 06:02.862
It’s fine. It’ll feel cooler soon.

06:09.118 --> 06:10.078
Here we are.

06:14.999 --> 06:17.627
Welcome. Two participants, correct?

06:17.710 --> 06:20.379
Yes, we’re looking forward to it.

06:20.880 --> 06:22.131
Likewise.

06:22.215 --> 06:25.593
Turn off the lanterns
and use these instead.

06:30.014 --> 06:33.434
<i>She's beautiful,</i>
<i>but quite an aged palace woman.</i>

06:34.102 --> 06:35.770
Now, let’s begin.

06:38.856 --> 06:42.401
This place was used
during the previous emperor’s reign.

06:43.152 --> 06:46.572
There are far fewer palace women
now than back then,

06:48.866 --> 06:50.910
but for something like this, it’s perfect.

06:55.623 --> 06:57.834
Take a seat wherever there’s space.

07:03.840 --> 07:05.174
Everyone’s here.

07:06.592 --> 07:11.013
<i>Gathering 12 people in a closed room</i>
<i>on such a hot day…</i>

07:11.639 --> 07:15.726
Everyone, are you ready for the stories?

07:16.436 --> 07:21.232
Tonight, let's enjoy 13 chilling tales.

07:21.941 --> 07:23.401
<i>Thirteen tales?</i>

07:26.988 --> 07:28.865
And so…

07:29.532 --> 07:31.659
Night after night,
at the moat by the north gate,

07:31.742 --> 07:34.871
there was a figure of a maid
repeatedly throwing herself in.

07:34.954 --> 07:39.167
Feeling pity, a palace woman
floated flowers in the water,

07:39.250 --> 07:41.919
when suddenly from somewhere,
a voice could be heard…

07:42.503 --> 07:44.964
Startled, she looked into the moat, and…

07:45.047 --> 07:47.592
the maid’s pale face
floated to the surface.

07:47.675 --> 07:50.261
As the palace woman panicked
and tried to flee,

07:50.344 --> 07:52.180
she was suddenly grabbed by the leg.

07:54.056 --> 07:57.226
The maid, crawling out of the water, said…

07:57.977 --> 08:02.648
"That day, the one who pushed me in…

08:05.276 --> 08:07.320
Was it you?!"

08:10.948 --> 08:13.701
<i>This sounds like a story</i>
<i>I've heard somewhere before.</i>

08:14.994 --> 08:18.122
<i>She's scared, but it seems</i>
<i>she's enjoying it.</i>

08:23.044 --> 08:26.797
<i>Apparently, this event involves</i>
<i>telling ghost stories in order of seating</i>

08:26.881 --> 08:30.218
<i>and blowing out a candle</i>
<i>after finishing each tale.</i>

08:30.885 --> 08:34.972
<i>However, most of the stories</i>
<i>are just rear palace rumors.</i>

08:35.056 --> 08:36.974
<i>Not exactly chilling to the bone.</i>

08:40.811 --> 08:43.356
<i>After all, there's little entertainment</i>
<i>in the rear palace.</i>

08:43.856 --> 08:46.651
<i>That's probably why</i>
<i>such gatherings are permitted.</i>

08:48.819 --> 08:51.614
-Good evening.
-Shisui.

08:51.697 --> 08:53.616
-Want some?
-I'll have a piece.

08:59.205 --> 09:00.540
Now then…

09:01.374 --> 09:04.585
This is a story from my hometown.

09:06.295 --> 09:07.421
<i>There was a forest,</i>

09:07.505 --> 09:11.592
<i>which had long been said</i>
<i>to be forbidden to enter.</i>

09:12.343 --> 09:14.136
<i>Anyone who entered would be cursed,</i>

09:14.220 --> 09:16.681
<i>and their soul would be</i>
<i>devoured by a demon.</i>

09:17.181 --> 09:19.100
<i>But one day,</i>

09:19.183 --> 09:22.478
<i>a child broke this taboo.</i>

09:23.271 --> 09:25.523
<i>That year, crops had failed,</i>

09:25.606 --> 09:28.025
<i>and the child, starving beyond endurance,</i>

09:28.109 --> 09:31.362
<i>entered the forest in search of food.</i>

09:33.990 --> 09:36.367
<i>The child told his mother,</i>

09:36.993 --> 09:38.911
<i>"I'll tell you something good.</i>

09:38.995 --> 09:41.706
<i>There’s plenty of food in that forest."</i>

09:42.873 --> 09:46.836
<i>However, when the villagers learned</i>
<i>that the child had entered the forest,</i>

09:46.919 --> 09:49.130
<i>the mother and child</i>
<i>were cast out from the village.</i>

09:49.964 --> 09:52.800
<i>Isolated, with nothing to eat,</i>

09:52.883 --> 09:55.011
<i>they grew frail and weak.</i>

09:55.094 --> 09:57.805
<i>Yet, no one reached out to help them.</i>

09:59.223 --> 10:00.850
<i>One night,</i>

10:01.350 --> 10:02.643
<i>someone saw a flickering light</i>

10:02.727 --> 10:06.439
<i>enter the mother and child's home.</i>

10:07.273 --> 10:10.234
<i>The next day, upon hearing the news,</i>

10:10.318 --> 10:11.944
<i>the village chief</i>
<i>went to visit their home.</i>

10:13.070 --> 10:14.905
<i>But the child was already dead,</i>

10:14.989 --> 10:17.158
<i>and the mother was on the verge of death.</i>

10:18.326 --> 10:20.161
<i>With her last breath,</i>
<i>she said to the village chief,</i>

10:21.537 --> 10:24.665
<i>"I'll tell you something good…</i>"

10:25.333 --> 10:29.128
<i>And with that, she died.</i>

10:29.837 --> 10:33.841
<i>Her face bore an eerie smile.</i>

10:34.717 --> 10:38.679
<i>In the end, no one knew</i>
<i>what she had meant to say.</i>

10:38.763 --> 10:41.974
<i>Even now, the forest is feared</i>
<i>as a forbidden land.</i>

10:42.058 --> 10:43.809
<i>And they say that a demon appears</i>

10:43.893 --> 10:45.645
<i>at the homes of those who break the taboo,</i>

10:45.728 --> 10:48.356
<i>devouring their souls.</i>

10:51.525 --> 10:55.279
-Hmm, I see…
-See what?

10:55.363 --> 10:56.906
I’ll tell you later.

10:59.075 --> 11:01.077
<i>I'm kinda sleepy…</i>

11:01.160 --> 11:03.245
<i>There are so many people</i>
<i>in such a small space.</i>

11:03.329 --> 11:05.623
<i>I’m feeling dizzy from the crowd.</i>

11:05.706 --> 11:07.750
Now it's your turn.

11:08.459 --> 11:10.211
Okay!

11:12.797 --> 11:17.593
This is a story from a far,
far eastern land.

11:19.178 --> 11:21.347
<i>A certain monk,</i>

11:21.430 --> 11:24.725
<i>on his way back after conducting</i>
<i>a funeral in a distant place,</i>

11:24.809 --> 11:27.478
<i>realized that night had already fallen.</i>

11:28.521 --> 11:31.440
<i>The area was an open plain</i>
<i>covered in silver grass,</i>

11:31.524 --> 11:34.485
<i>and it seemed that a pack of stray dogs</i>
<i>were lurking nearby.</i>

11:35.111 --> 11:38.072
<i>As the anxious monk looked around,</i>

11:38.155 --> 11:40.491
<i>he spotted an old, worn-down house.</i>

11:43.285 --> 11:45.830
Pardon the late hour. Is anyone home?

11:47.415 --> 11:49.708
What brings you here, dear monk?

11:49.792 --> 11:53.045
Before I could cross the mountain,
night fell…

11:53.129 --> 11:55.256
If you wouldn’t mind,
even a corner of the barn would do.

11:55.339 --> 11:57.216
Could you let me stay for just one night?

11:57.299 --> 12:01.512
Oh my… You must be exhausted.

12:03.389 --> 12:05.266
<i>The wife fed him</i>

12:05.933 --> 12:08.269
<i>and even prepared</i>
<i>a sleeping place for him.</i>

12:09.145 --> 12:11.605
<i>Moved by her heartfelt hospitality,</i>

12:11.689 --> 12:14.233
<i>the monk, who had</i>
<i>nothing to offer in return,</i>

12:14.316 --> 12:17.278
<i>decided to at least recite a sutra</i>
<i>as a token of gratitude.</i>

12:24.034 --> 12:25.578
<i>Is that the sound of a bell?</i>

12:26.537 --> 12:29.206
<i>No… It sounds like a bell, but…</i>

12:29.957 --> 12:32.168
<i>Is this… a human voice?</i>

12:32.835 --> 12:35.171
So, what will you do?

12:35.254 --> 12:37.423
Nothing. It should be fine as it is.

12:37.506 --> 12:40.092
No, that won’t do!

12:40.176 --> 12:42.011
I don’t want to be alone.

12:42.094 --> 12:44.305
Then, what do you plan to do?!

12:45.014 --> 12:46.724
I can't take this anymore…

12:48.100 --> 12:52.021
<i>Are they arguing? Should I step in?</i>

12:52.104 --> 12:56.400
<i>No. I mustn’t interfere.</i>
<i>I just have that feeling…</i>

12:56.484 --> 12:59.862
-That monk… we'll use him instead.
-I guess there’s no other way…

13:01.614 --> 13:04.450
Alright, let's do this.

13:07.077 --> 13:09.622
Where is he? Where’s the monk?

13:21.383 --> 13:22.760
Did he escape?

13:25.387 --> 13:27.806
He’s not here. He’s gone!

13:27.890 --> 13:31.644
I have to find him. Otherwise, I…

13:31.727 --> 13:33.145
I…

13:39.860 --> 13:41.153
<i>The monk</i>

13:41.237 --> 13:45.491
<i>continued chanting the sutra,</i>
<i>until the sounds of chewing stopped.</i>

13:46.450 --> 13:50.454
<i>When the noise ceased,</i>
<i>the monk stepped outside.</i>

13:51.080 --> 13:54.708
<i>The young couple was nowhere to be seen,</i>
<i>and in their place…</i>

13:56.001 --> 13:58.254
<i>only insect wings lay scattered</i>
<i>on the ground.</i>

13:58.879 --> 14:02.508
The monk quietly pressed his hands
together in prayer

14:03.717 --> 14:05.970
and continued walking,
chanting the sutra, until dawn.

14:07.096 --> 14:09.557
<i>She's really good at telling stories.</i>

14:09.640 --> 14:11.475
<i>It’s like she's</i>
<i>a completely different person.</i>

14:13.519 --> 14:14.979
<i>This side profile…</i>

14:15.729 --> 14:18.482
<i>Feels like I’ve seen it somewhere before…</i>

14:21.151 --> 14:22.820
Maomao. You’re up next.

14:23.571 --> 14:24.613
Oh, right…

14:25.239 --> 14:27.157
<i>What should I talk about…?</i>

14:28.993 --> 14:31.328
My foster father once told me a story.

14:31.412 --> 14:34.915
There was a rumor that ghostly fireballs
appeared in the graveyard.

14:36.542 --> 14:38.210
<i>It sounded suspicious,</i>

14:38.294 --> 14:41.714
<i>so a group of brave young men</i>
<i>went to investigate.</i>

14:43.132 --> 14:44.300
<i>And what they found was…</i>

14:49.847 --> 14:52.057
<i>A man from the same town,</i>

14:52.141 --> 14:54.685
<i>walking with a torch in his hand.</i>

14:56.854 --> 14:58.814
-That’s it?
-Yes.

14:59.315 --> 15:01.483
The man was a grave robber,

15:01.567 --> 15:03.652
trapped by a sinister curse.

15:03.736 --> 15:06.655
<i>He would dig up graves,</i>
<i>cut open corpses’ bellies,</i>

15:07.239 --> 15:09.992
and take human livers,
said to cure rare diseases--

15:10.075 --> 15:11.243
Enough!

15:12.578 --> 15:14.246
That’s all…

15:16.832 --> 15:19.376
You're next, Lady Yinghua.

15:21.211 --> 15:23.255
Well…

15:23.923 --> 15:26.884
There was once a man…

15:26.967 --> 15:29.762
No, an old woman…?

15:30.429 --> 15:31.764
And then… Um…

15:31.847 --> 15:33.599
So then… Um…

15:38.479 --> 15:41.023
Then, I’ll go next.

15:41.941 --> 15:43.233
<i>Come to think of it,</i>

15:43.317 --> 15:46.528
<i>that palace woman mentioned</i>
<i>"13 tales" at the start.</i>

15:47.363 --> 15:50.991
<i>But there are only 12 of us here.</i>
<i>What does she mean?</i>

15:51.075 --> 15:53.535
This is a story from
the previous emperor’s time.

15:54.119 --> 15:57.247
Back then, the rear palace kept growing,

15:57.331 --> 16:00.042
and new quarters
were constantly being added.

16:00.125 --> 16:02.002
For what reason?

16:02.670 --> 16:05.631
The Grand Empress Dowager,

16:05.714 --> 16:08.592
who wielded immense power at that time,

16:08.676 --> 16:13.055
was gathering girls to match
the emperor’s tastes.

16:15.432 --> 16:16.684
<i>What…?</i>

16:16.767 --> 16:18.268
The previous emperor

16:18.352 --> 16:22.189
would choose young girls, barely of age,
and take their innocence.

16:23.273 --> 16:25.234
<i>The girls, once taken,</i>

16:25.317 --> 16:27.987
<i>were never allowed to leave,</i>

16:28.070 --> 16:30.197
<i>spending their days in confinement.</i>

16:30.990 --> 16:34.702
One of them became pregnant

16:35.494 --> 16:37.705
and pleaded with the emperor.

16:38.664 --> 16:42.209
But she was never allowed
to leave the rear palace,

16:42.292 --> 16:44.336
and just before she died,
she spoke her last words…

16:47.214 --> 16:50.175
"Next… it will be your turn!"

16:51.927 --> 16:52.761
Maomao!

16:55.848 --> 16:57.766
<i>No wonder my head feels foggy!</i>

16:58.267 --> 16:59.852
Lady Yinghua, Shisui!

16:59.935 --> 17:02.813
Move the weakened palace women
near the windows and doors!

17:02.896 --> 17:05.024
What on earth is going on?

17:05.107 --> 17:07.484
Hurry! The lingering flames are releasing

17:08.152 --> 17:10.988
toxic air that's filling the room.

17:12.031 --> 17:13.157
Got it!

17:18.495 --> 17:20.456
<i>I realized it too late…</i>

17:23.000 --> 17:25.377
And I was so close.

17:29.381 --> 17:30.841
<i>That palace woman…</i>

17:36.472 --> 17:38.766
Things got pretty chaotic, huh?

17:38.849 --> 17:41.143
And the hostess disappeared too.

17:42.019 --> 17:42.978
Maomao!

17:43.979 --> 17:45.355
The girl from earlier…

17:45.439 --> 17:47.191
She's an acquaintance of mine.

17:47.775 --> 17:50.652
Hey, Maomao.
What was that story about earlier?

17:51.236 --> 17:52.237
Earlier?

17:52.321 --> 17:54.865
You know, the story
about the Forbidden Forest.

17:57.284 --> 18:00.287
The "Forbidden Forest"
is just a superstition,

18:00.370 --> 18:04.583
but I can’t say for sure that
there’s no reason it became taboo.

18:06.001 --> 18:08.587
The forest is rich in food,

18:08.670 --> 18:10.881
but it’s also full of things
that aren’t edible.

18:12.132 --> 18:14.093
<i>People from other lands would come,</i>

18:14.176 --> 18:17.721
<i>eat things from the forest and fall ill.</i>

18:18.555 --> 18:22.059
<i>And so, people started saying,</i>
<i>"You mustn’t eat anything</i>

18:22.142 --> 18:23.727
<i>from the forest carelessly."</i>

18:24.394 --> 18:28.357
<i>Over time, that became a forbidden rule.</i>

18:28.440 --> 18:30.734
<i>And when famines occurred later on,</i>

18:30.818 --> 18:35.280
people could no longer tell which foods
were safe and which were not.

18:36.073 --> 18:39.910
<i>The mother and child in that story were</i>
<i>starving during a year of poor harvest.</i>

18:40.452 --> 18:44.540
<i>Since they were breaking the rules,</i>
<i>they must have entered the forest at dusk,</i>

18:44.623 --> 18:48.794
<i>gathered food,</i>
<i>and returned home after nightfall.</i>

18:49.711 --> 18:51.463
<i>There’s a mushroom called</i>
<i>"moonlight mushroom,"</i>

18:51.547 --> 18:53.966
<i>a type of mushroom</i>
<i>that resembles oyster mushrooms.</i>

18:54.049 --> 18:56.635
<i>It looks very delicious,</i>
<i>but it's poisonous.</i>

18:56.718 --> 18:59.054
<i>And it has a unique trait,</i>
<i>it glows in the dark.</i>

19:00.139 --> 19:03.851
<i>If a villager had seen</i>
<i>someone walking at night from afar,</i>

19:03.934 --> 19:06.061
<i>they might have mistaken it</i>
<i>for a ghostly spirit.</i>

19:07.062 --> 19:09.106
<i>The poison isn’t very strong,</i>

19:09.189 --> 19:12.985
<i>but if a starving, weakened mother</i>
<i>and child ate it…?</i>

19:16.864 --> 19:21.076
<i>Perhaps, in her final moments,</i>
<i>the mother wanted to say this…</i>

19:22.452 --> 19:26.165
<i>"There are delicious mushrooms</i>
<i>in the forest…"</i>

19:27.708 --> 19:30.043
<i>She meant to say that</i>
<i>as a way to get back at the villagers</i>

19:30.127 --> 19:32.087
<i>who abandoned her and her child.</i>

19:32.880 --> 19:34.548
So that’s what it was!

19:34.631 --> 19:36.925
Yeah, now it all makes sense!

19:37.009 --> 19:39.052
Well, I’m heading back this way!

19:42.014 --> 19:44.725
Once you understand the truth behind it,
it's nothing special.

19:45.601 --> 19:48.937
I'm sure other stories have
similar hidden meanings too.

19:50.272 --> 19:52.399
Well, who knows?

19:52.482 --> 19:54.943
What do you mean by that?

19:57.321 --> 19:58.655
I'm back.

19:58.739 --> 20:01.575
Oh, that was quicker than I expected.

20:01.658 --> 20:03.994
There was a bit of commotion.

20:04.077 --> 20:05.621
Well, as expected…

20:05.704 --> 20:09.333
When someone inexperienced
is in charge, things happen.

20:09.875 --> 20:11.168
Inexperienced?

20:11.251 --> 20:14.171
The palace woman who handled it
until last year passed away,

20:14.254 --> 20:17.424
so I was worried about
who would take over this year.

20:18.842 --> 20:22.596
She was a very thoughtful and kind person.
I was taken care of by her too.

20:22.679 --> 20:25.432
In the end, she never
got to leave the rear palace.

20:26.099 --> 20:29.436
<i>Actually, she was once favored</i>
<i>by the previous emperor,</i>

20:29.519 --> 20:32.648
<i>and that gathering was</i>
<i>her only source of joy.</i>

20:33.732 --> 20:36.693
The fact that the gathering ceased
the year after she passed away,

20:36.777 --> 20:38.779
I always found that rather unsettling.

20:39.613 --> 20:42.282
I'm glad someone decided to continue it.

20:44.952 --> 20:46.370
That story…

20:48.914 --> 20:53.877
The previous emperor chose young girls,
barely of age, taking their innocence.

20:54.503 --> 20:58.298
<i>The girls, once taken,</i>
<i>were never allowed to leave…</i>

21:00.133 --> 21:04.054
<i>Was that palace woman's</i>
<i>story her own tale?</i>

21:04.805 --> 21:08.600
<i>Or was it a cruel jest by someone</i>
<i>who knew the truth?</i>

21:11.687 --> 21:15.565
<i>The world is full of things</i>
<i>we may never understand.</i>

21:16.733 --> 21:17.859
Tonight,

21:17.943 --> 21:21.571
let's enjoy 13 chilling tales.

21:22.990 --> 21:26.493
<i>At that time, at that place,</i>
<i>even counting the elder palace woman,</i>

21:26.576 --> 21:28.578
<i>there were only 12 people present.</i>

21:29.204 --> 21:30.372
<i>For now,</i>

21:30.455 --> 21:33.917
<i>I'm glad we didn’t end up</i>
<i>becoming the 13th ghost story.</i>

21:35.127 --> 21:37.087
-Maomao!
-Yes?

21:37.713 --> 21:41.008
Can I sleep with you tonight?!

21:46.555 --> 21:48.640
<i>Rather than a spine-chilling night,</i>

21:48.724 --> 21:51.685
<i>it became a restless,</i>
<i>uncomfortable one instead…</i>

21:52.853 --> 21:55.355
<i>-Too hot to bear.</i>
-What is…this…?

23:46.133 --> 23:50.512
NEXT EPISODE PREVIEW

23:58.186 --> 23:59.771
<i>The next episode is "The Hunt."</i>

23:59.855 --> 24:01.690
